Package: landisR.harvest
Type: Package
Title: Experimental Native Living Biomass Harvest for landisR
Version: 0.0.0.9028
Authors@R: person("LANDIS-R", "Development", email="landisR-maintainer@example.invalid", role=c("aut","cre"))
Description: Experimental native living-cohort removal and deterministic whole-stand allocation using the shared CSR forest state of landisR. H04-C2 adds deterministic
                  RegulateAges, inclusive MaximumAge and ForestTypeTable. H04-C3b adds a separate seed-plus-offset MT19937 Random pilot, with exact historical results
                  in selected LANDIS-II v7 fixtures. Full shared RNG coupling and other LANDIS-II modules remain in qualification. H04-D2 adds sparse rook neighbor
                  topology and sequential MA harvest history for SiteSelection Complete. H04-E2 adds multi-prescription weighted stochastic selection and one RNG draw
                  per harvest event for Complete site-selection. H04-D2 remains a frozen regression reference; stochastic multi-annual coupled RNG remains to be
                  qualified. H04-E3 adds an experimental fused CSR native pilot for mixed MaxCohortAge Complete prescriptions with per-prescription adjacency, harvest
                  history, and one Required ForestType rule; only first-step deterministic-ranking references are targeted. H04-E4b fixes ForestType validation after
                  an expected species goes locally or globally absent: fixed catalog replaces the live CSR maximum ID. H04-E4d adds experimental uniform Random ranking
                  within mixed Complete prescriptions and sparse no-effect EventLog semantics with ecological, not seed-identity, validation. H04-E4g credits only
                  sites with positive biomass removal toward Complete area quotas when treatment rules are supplied. Adds CompleteStandSpread, PartialStandSpread and
                  PatchCutting to the native area-quota planner. Adds configurable neighboring-stand set-aside and scheduled repeat harvests. Supports cell-level
                  minimum time since damage.
